 "final_message": "I've done all 12 items, and the 6 tests pass (the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones). I didn't write tests for the other fixes.\n\n**Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow their SPEC sections.\n- **Parsing errors:** `parse_session_log` raises `ValueError` with `line N` for a wrong field count or a non-integer day. SPEC doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty, so I made that raise `ValueError` with `line N` too.\n\n**Items 9\u201310:** I added `test_conversion_rate_none_is_not_converted` and `test_dedupe_sessions_keeps_last_duplicate` to `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n\n**Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries, and there is a new `daily_conversion_counts` entry. I also reworded the `dedupe_sessions` entry, which you didn't ask for, to say it keeps the last session per `id`.\n\n**Item 12:** The rest of the package had three more departures from SPEC, which I fixed:\n- `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups, breaks ties by group name, and returns nothing for `n <= 0`.\n- `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and orders keys by group name.\n- `longest_flag_streak` now resets the run when it hits a day with no conversions. Before, it counted all non-zero days as one run.",
